ype":"text","url":"/docs/mobile#features","content":"Offline support with background sync"},"464":{"id":"/docs/openapi","page_id":"/docs/openapi","type":"page","content":"OpenAPI","breadcrumbs":["Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/openapi"},"465":{"id":"/docs/openapi-0","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi","content":"Import the Mosaic OpenAPI 3.1 document into Swagger Editor or Postman"},"466":{"id":"/docs/openapi-1","page_id":"/docs/openapi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/openapi#openapi","content":"OpenAPI"},"467":{"id":"/docs/openapi-2","page_id":"/docs/openapi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/openapi#import-into-swagger-editor","content":"Import into Swagger Editor"},"468":{"id":"/docs/openapi-3","page_id":"/docs/openapi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/openapi#import-into-postman","content":"Import into Postman"},"469":{"id":"/docs/openapi-4","page_id":"/docs/openapi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/openapi#server-url-and-local-access","content":"Server URL and Local Access"},"470":{"id":"/docs/openapi-5","page_id":"/docs/openapi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/openapi#example-request","content":"Example Request"},"471":{"id":"/docs/openapi-6","page_id":"/docs/openapi","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/openapi#notes","content":"Notes"},"472":{"id":"/docs/openapi-7","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#openapi","content":"The running server publishes its HTTP contract as an **OpenAPI 3.1** document:"},"473":{"id":"/docs/openapi-8","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#openapi","content":"Live endpoint: `http://localhost:8080/openapi.json`"},"474":{"id":"/docs/openapi-9","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#openapi","content":"Spec source in this repository: `server-go/internal/httpapi/openapi.json`"},"475":{"id":"/docs/openapi-10","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#openapi","content":"`GET /openapi.json` is public — it needs no authentication and returns JSON. The\nport follows `PORT`, so a server started on another port serves it there instead."},"476":{"id":"/docs/openapi-11","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#openapi","content":"The document is embedded into the server binary at build time (`//go:embed`). An\nimage built before this entry was added returns `404` for `/openapi.json`; the\nendpoint appears only after the server is redeployed with the new image."},"477":{"id":"/docs/openapi-12","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#import-into-swagger-editor","content":"Open editor.swagger.io."},"478":{"id":"/docs/openapi-13","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#import-into-swagger-editor","content":"Choose **File → Import URL** (or paste a saved copy with **File → Import File**)."},"479":{"id":"/docs/openapi-14","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#import-into-swagger-editor","content":"Enter `http://localhost:8080/openapi.json`."},"480":{"id":"/docs/openapi-15","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#import-into-swagger-editor","content":"A successful import lists the operations and reports no validation errors.\nSwagger Editor validates and browses the document; whether its **Authorize** and\ntry-it-out calls reach your server depends on the editor's network access and on\nthe server URL you set, so treat those calls as best-effort. For real requests,\nuse Swagger UI or Postman running where it can reach the server."},"481":{"id":"/docs/openapi-16","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#import-into-postman","content":"In Postman, choose **Import**."},"482":{"id":"/docs/openapi-17","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#import-into-postman","content":"Select the **Link** tab and enter `http://localhost:8080/openapi.json`, or the\n**File** tab and pick a saved copy of the JSON."},"483":{"id":"/docs/openapi-18","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#import-into-postman","content":"Import as a new collection, then point the collection at your server before\nsending requests."},"484":{"id":"/docs/openapi-19","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#server-url-and-local-access","content":"The document declares a relative server URL (`/`). When a remote tool imports it,\nthat relative value resolves against the tool's own origin, so requests would\ntarget the tool's site rather than Mosaic. Set the server URL explicitly to your\ninstance — for example `http://localhost:8080` in Swagger UI or Swagger Editor,\nor a `baseUrl` collection variable in Postman."},"485":{"id":"/docs/openapi-20","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#server-url-and-local-access","content":"Local access has the usual limits:"},"486":{"id":"/docs/openapi-21","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#server-url-and-local-access","content":"A server on plain HTTP at `http://localhost:8080` is reachable only from the\nsame machine. From another device, browse to the host's LAN address; the\ncalling page's origin (for example `https://editor.swagger.io` or your own UI\norigin) must be listed in `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`. The server's LAN address is not an\norigin and does not belong there."},"487":{"id":"/docs/openapi-22","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#server-url-and-local-access","content":"Browsers treat `http://localhost` and `http://127.0.0.1` as potentially\ntrustworthy, so an HTTPS page can usually still fetch `http://localhost`. The\nblock applies to other plain-HTTP targets, such as a LAN IP: a page served over\nHTTPS cannot fetch those. Download the JSON and import the file, or serve your\nserver over HTTPS."},"488":{"id":"/docs/openapi-23","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#server-url-and-local-access","content":"An `Authorization` header makes the browser send a CORS preflight. The calling\norigin must be allowed by the server's CORS policy; `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` is\npermissive only when it is empty (development)."},"489":{"id":"/docs/openapi-24","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#example-request","content":"Fictional values, unless you substitute your own:"},"490":{"id":"/docs/openapi-25","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#example-request","content":"`GET /api/memos` returns a paginated envelope (`items`, `total`, `page`,\n`pageSize`, `totalPages`); `GET /api/memos/search` uses a different shape. The\ndocument is the source of truth for each response."},"491":{"id":"/docs/openapi-26","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#notes","content":"The document is emitted by the server directly — no extra tooling or\ndependency is required to produce or read it."},"492":{"id":"/docs/openapi-27","page_id":"/docs/openapi","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/openapi#notes","content":"`docs/server-api.md` remains the prose reference for the same contract."},"493":{"id":"/docs/privacy","page_id":"/docs/privacy","type":"page","content":"Privacy & Data","breadcrumbs":["Documentation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/privacy"},"494":{"id":"/docs/privacy-0","page_id":"/docs/privacy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/privacy","content":"How Mosaic handles your data and privacy options"},"495":{"id":"/docs/privacy-1","page_id":"/docs/privacy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/privacy#privacy--data","content":"Privacy & Data"},"496":{"id":"/docs/privacy-2","page_id":"/docs/privacy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/privacy#data-ownership","content":"Data Ownership"},"497":{"id":"/docs/privacy-3","page_id":"/docs/privacy","type":"heading","tags":[],"